        "reported_material_gaps": [],
        "research_rationale": "Identity: the registered original is the Federal Register machine text of Executive Order 12584 (52 FR 5429, PDF page 11 of the 1987-02-23 issue; sha256 9ce8d3b6...), headed \"President’s Special Review Board\" in the OCR layer, which splits many words with stray spaces. It is signed February 19, 1987, which matches the census register row (1987-02-19, President's Special Review Board). The machine heading search did not resolve the heading; I confirmed it by reading the OCR heading line, which reads Executive Order 12584 of February 19, 1987. Text and inventory: one operative paragraph; it extends the time within which the Board may submit its findings and recommendations by amending section 2(b) of Executive Order 12575 (as amended), deleting the date February 19, 1987 and inserting February 26, 1987. The inventory is one clause and I confirm it. Ending: Executive Order 12610 (signed 1987-09-30, effective that day) revokes Executive Order 12575, the parent that the amendment changes; the amended provision cannot operate without its parent. The amendment itself was made when signed, and its effect (the changed report date) lives in section 2(b) of the parent until the parent ends; that is the reading of the owner ruling of 2026-10-21 on strike-and-insert amendments, disclosed as a reading. Original grade: Federal Register machine text.\nMember checks: {\"earlier_end_check\":\"Candidate earlier ends examined. (1) The parent order's own terms (section 4 of Executive Order 12575) end the Board 30 days after it submits its report; the extended report date of February 26, 1987 is a deadline, not an end, and no held source dates the actual report, so the owner ruling of 2026-10-21 on report deadlines applies and no own-terms end is claimed. (2) Executive Order 12610 is the only held instrument that names the parent; a search of the held corpus for the number 12584 found no other instrument naming this order, and the OFR disposition-note machine search has no hit for it. (3) No instrument before 12610 revokes the parent.\",\"independent_command_check\":\"The order has a single command, the amendment of the date in section 2(b) of Executive Order 12575. It gives no direction that outlives the parent order: its only effect is on the Board's report date.\",\"savings_check\":\"Executive Order 12610 sections 1 through 5 contain no wording that preserves Executive Order 12575 or its amendments: section 1 continues other committees, section 2 concerns only those, and section 3(g) revokes the parent without exception.\",\"scope_check\":\"One clause. Executive Order 12610 section 3(g) revokes Executive Order 12575 in full, without any exception; it does not name Executive Order 12584, so the end rests on the parent being revoked, disclosed as a parent-as-amended reading. I read sections 1 through 5 of Executive Order 12610; section 4 supersedes Executive Order 12534 and does not bear on this order.\"}",
